---
/**
 * About block, from Figma 1:15789.
 *
 * The reference heads this section with a handwritten "Good
 * morning". It is the one warm note in an otherwise instrument-like
 * page, and it works because it is time-aware: it greets you
 * according to YOUR clock, so it reads as addressed rather than
 * decorative.
 *
 * Server-rendered from the site's own timezone first, then
 * corrected client-side to the visitor's. Without the correction a
 * visitor in London gets "Good evening" at breakfast, which is
 * worse than no greeting at all.
 */
import { site } from "../../config/site";

const hour = Number(
  new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
    timeZone: site.timezone,
    hour: "2-digit",
    hour12: false,
  }).format(new Date())
);
const initial =
  hour < 5 ? "Still up?" : hour < 12 ? "Good morning" : hour < 18 ? "Good afternoon" : "Good evening";
---

{/*
  FOUR BULLETS BECAME ONE STATEMENT.

  The four paragraphs that used to live here said, in order: the two
  degrees, why the combination matters, that measurement is the point,
  and what he is doing now. All true, all at 16px, all weighted the
  same, so a reader skimming took none of it.

  The one idea worth stopping for is the second: the machine learning
  is attached to something that keeps running whether or not the model
  is right. That is now the whole block, at --text-lead, at two lines
  on mobile and three on desktop. The rest of the facts are not
  deleted, they are demoted: the degrees are already in the identity
  grid above, and the current work now sits on one supporting line.

  This is the hierarchy fix in one block. The lead is three scale
  steps above the line under it, so the eye lands on the claim first
  and reaches the detail second, which is the order they matter in.
*/}
<div>
  <p class="label" data-greeting>{initial}</p>

  <p class="lead mt-3">
    Most of my machine learning ends up on a machine that keeps running
    whether or not the model is right.
  </p>

  <p class="prose-measure mt-5 text-body text-ink-2">
    Which is why every project here states its baseline, its evaluation set,
    and the conditions under which it fails. A metric without those three is
    a decoration. Currently: bearing-fault detection on live CNC spindles at
    the <span class="text-ink">Smart Manufacturing Lab</span>.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  /* Bullets are drawn rather than list-style, so the dot can be a
     token colour and sit on the first line's optical centre. */
  .bullet {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.125rem;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16px;
  }
  .bullet::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.125rem;
    top: 0.625rem;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 999px
    ;
    background-color: var(--color-ink-4);
  }
</style>

<script>
  /* Correct the greeting to the VISITOR's clock. The server can
     only know Ashutosh's timezone, and this line is addressed to
     whoever is reading it. */
  const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-greeting]");
  if (el) {
    const h = new Date().getHours();
    el.textContent =
      h < 5
        ? "Still up?"
        : h < 12
          ? "Good morning"
          : h < 18
            ? "Good afternoon"
            : "Good evening";
  }
</script>
